k><name>MITSUBA CORP</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NOZUE YUTAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UCHIYAMA HIDEKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITSUBA CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NOZUE, YUTAKA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UCHIYAMA, HIDEKAZU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NOZUE YUTAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UCHIYAMA HIDEKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NOZUE, YUTAKA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UCHIYAMA, HIDEKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A brushless motor comprises a stator (3) with an armature coil (11) wound on it, a rotor (5) capable of rotating inside or outside the stator (3), a ring magnet (24) and a sensor unit (25) which detect the position of the rotor, a motor driver (31) for energizing the armature coil (11) so that a rotating magnetic field may appear according to the rotor position.  The rotor (5) comprises a field magnet that includes a plurality of permanent magnets (9) magnetized to the same pole and a plurality of control poles (10) of magnetic material interposed between the permanent magnets (9).  The stator (3) is provided with a field coil (13) that forms a closed magnetic circuit passing through the control poles (10).  The characteristics of the motor are controlled without sacrificing motor efficiency by controlling the direction and amount of current for energizing the field coil (13).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un moteur sans balais qui comporte un stator (3) équipé d'une bobine d'armature (11) enroulée sur celui-ci, un rotor (5) capable de tourner à l'intérieur ou à l'extérieur du stator (3), un aimant annulaire (24) et un dispositif de détection (25) qui détecte la position du rotor, un organe d'entraînement (31) de moteur pour exciter la bobine d'armature (11) de façon à produire un champ magnétique rotatif en fonction de la position du rotor. Le rotor (5) comporte un inducteur comportant plusieurs aimants (9) permanents magnétisés sur le même pôle, et plusieurs pôles (10) de commande en matière magnétique placés entre les aimants (9) permanents. Le stator (3) est pourvu d'un enroulement inducteur (13) qui forme un circuit magnétique fermé traversant les pôles (10) de commande. On règle les caractéristiques du moteur sans perte de rendement de celui-ci en réglant la direction et la quantité de courant utilisée pour exciter l'enroulement inducteur (13).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>